sub:assertion {
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/levin-2024-anthrobots-11> delphi:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/levin-2024-anthrobots-11--grok> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/levin-2024-anthrobots-11--grok> a delphi:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Grok 4.7 on levin-2024-anthrobots-11: needs-new-data, resolvability 0.30" ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.2.0> ;
    delphi:assessmentType "dataset-resolvability/0.2.0" ;
    delphi:hasScore "0.297"^^xsd:double ;
    delphi:hasVerdict "needs-new-data" ;
    delphi:hasConfidence "0.66"^^xsd:double ;
    dct:description "Within-bot consistency is measurable from the same five-hour tracks as the transition matrix, and those tracks are not public. Even with them, rare switching would not show that bots self-organize into types rather than simply keeping the geometry they had when recording started. The stability half is waiting on data; the self-organization wording stays underdetermined." ;
    rdfs:comment "Proposed test with existing data: For each bot, compute the fraction of its 30-second segments that stay in one movement class and the rate of switches between circular and linear. High within-bot consistency and rare cross-class switches would support stable individual types; frequent switching by the same bot would refute a lasting fingerprint. Separating active self-organization from a type fixed by the initial cilia pattern needs early-time tracks the consistency score alone does not provide." ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-grok-4.7-high-fast> ;
    delphi:evidenceAgainst "Per-bot identity of segments is not in a public file.", "Low switching does not distinguish self-organization from a type fixed at release by cilia geometry.", "A fingerprint is only as discrete as the upstream cluster boundaries." .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/levin-2024-anthrobots-11--grok--operationalizability> a delphi:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Operationalizability of levin-2024-anthrobots-11 by Grok 4.7: 0.68" ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.2.0-operationalizability> ;
